docs(database): lock DB10 durability scope

DB10-CP0. Reconciles the DB9 handoff from Git rather than from its report,
locks the DB10 acceptance-audit scope against the roadmap, and registers
every durability parameter and every table before any tooling is written.

- DB9 closed at 07a06ef across 8 commits; the report described the 8th
  without naming it. Addendum, not a blocker.
- DB9 tally corrected: 63 unique scope rows, 33 deferred, not 64/34.
  PERF-R33 was counted twice.
- The amended commit 623eb78 is reconciled additively and the no-amend rule
  is restated as absolute in DB6_MIGRATION_GOVERNANCE.md (DEV-GOV-001).
- All 33 deferred DB9 rows classified A-F: 1 is DB10 scope, 30 are
  application-feature handoffs, 2 are future production validation, 0 block.
- 78/78 tables classified for durability, retention and PII, verified
  against the live catalog. The S24 retention_exempt policy is broader than
  the retention policy, so the job must use a code-level allowlist.
- Every retention duration and both recovery objectives stay DEFERRED with
  a named owner. Backup encryption is marked production-blocking.
